        <div class="col-lg-8 col-md-8 col-sm-8 col-xs-12 content">
            <article>
                <div class="tn-pagetitle show" aria-hidden="false">
    <h1>Pending and Final Permit Documents for Review</h1>
    

</div>

                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-cta parbase">
    <a href="/environment/program-areas/solid-waste.html" class="text-button icon-right-1" alt="Waste Management Branch Main Page">Waste Management Branch Main Page</a>


</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <h2>Pending Permits</h2>
<p>This section contains documents for facilities that have permit applications open for review and public comment.</p>

    
    

</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <h3>Virtual Participation Instructions and Guidance</h3>
<p>For participation in public meetings/hearings virtually/telephone details can be found under the Join Meeting tab or More Information tabs above, on the program&#39;s pending documents pages, and public hearing calendar pages.</p>

    
    

</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-linkbuttons"><div>
	
        <div>
            
            
                <a href="/content/dam/tn/environment/solid-waste/documents/public-notices/ppo_webex_instructions.pdf" target="_blank" class="button standard">WebEx Instructions for Virtual Public Hearings</a>
            
        </div>
	
</div></div>


    
    
    <div class="containers tn-accordion parbase">
    <div class="accordion" id="accordion-5a3338dc32ab4bb785e49a724c0393f1">
        

        
            

            
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    

                    
                        <div class="accordion-heading">
                            <span class="accordion-title">
                                <button class="accordion-button icon-angle-right collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-5a3338dc32ab4bb785e49a724c0393f1-0" aria-controls="collapse-5a3338dc32ab4bb785e49a724c0393f1-0" aria-expanded="false">
                                    PLTN Holdings, LLC for the PLTN Holdings Class II Landfill (IDL540000100).
                                </button>
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <div id="collapse-5a3338dc32ab4bb785e49a724c0393f1-0" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordion-5a3338dc32ab4bb785e49a724c0393f1">
                            <div class="accordion-body panel-body" tabindex="0">
                                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <p>The Tennessee Department of Environment and Conservation (TDEC), Division of Land Protection- Waste Management Branch (DLP- WMB), has tentatively decided to issue a solid waste disposal facility permit major modification to PLTN Holdings, LLC for the PLTN Holdings Class II Landfill (IDL540000100). The facility is located in McMinn County, at <span class="icon-location"></span>294 County Road 516, Englewood, Tennessee (latitude 35.3927/longitude -84.5171). This major modification addresses changes to the final contours, final cover system, and site drainage in order to close the landfill. This modification reduces the final contours and does not add additional air space or capacity to this landfill.</p>
<p>This permit would allow closure and post-closure care of the Class II disposal facility that was permitted for the disposal of excess system sand, slag, core room waste, mill room sand, core butts, pelletized plant dust, bottom drop, melt emission dust, and/or certain wastes having similar characteristics and approved in writing by TDEC. No hazardous wastes, as regulated by the Tennessee Hazardous Waste Management Act (Tennessee Code Annotated, Section 68-212-101, et. seq.) and the Rules adopted pursuant to the Act, shall be accepted for disposal at this facility. The official responsible for the operation of the facility is Monique Parker, CSP, PLTN Holdings, LLC, 42 E. Catawba Street, Belmont, NC 28012 <span class="icon-mobile"></span>(980) 701-9935.</p>
<p>DLP has made a preliminary determination that this proposal meets the applicable requirements of Tennessee Rule Chapter 0400-11-01, Solid Waste Processing and Disposal. Pending consideration of any comments received during the 45-day comment period ending on Tuesday, November 10, 2026 DLP intends to issue this permit modification.</p>
<p>DLP invites the public to review and submit comments on this proposal anytime during the 45-day comment period ending on <span class="icon-calendar-inv"></span>Tuesday, November 10, 2026. Paper copies are available by request at the <span class="icon-location"></span>TDEC Chattanooga Environmental Field Office, 1301 Riverfront Parkway, Suite #206, Chattanooga, TN 37402 <span class="icon-mobile"></span>(423) 634-5745 and the <span class="icon-location"></span>DLP Central Office, Davy Crockett Tower, 500 James Robertson Pkwy, 7th Floor, Nashville, TN 37243 <span class="icon-mobile"></span>(615) 532-0780.</p>
<p>To comment on the draft permit or request a public hearing on this issue, contact Abigail Moseley at DLP Central Office Davy Crockett Tower, 500 James Robertson Pkwy, 7th Floor, Nashville, TN 37243 <span class="icon-mobile">(</span>615) 917-5879, email <span class="icon-mail"></span><a title="email for Abigail Moseley" href="mailto:Abigail.Moseley&#64;tn.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Abigail.Moseley&#64;tn.gov</a>. Comments must be received by <span class="icon-clock"></span>4:30 p.m. CST on <span class="icon-calendar-inv"></span>Tuesday, November 10, 2026, to ensure consideration. A request for a public hearing must be in writing and state the nature of the issues proposed to be raised in the hearing. If a hearing is scheduled, another notice will be published at least 15 days in advance.</p>
<p>After considering all public comments, DLP will make a final decision to issue or deny the permit. DLP will provide notice of the final permit decision and a Response to Comments addressing all significant input received on the draft permit to the applicant and to each person who has submitted written comments. These documents will also be available online and at the repositories listed above.</p>
<p>Individuals with disabilities who wish to participate in the process may contact the DLP Human Resource (HR) liaison Rachel Meredith at <span class="icon-mobile"></span>(615) 532-0780 or <span class="icon-mail"></span><a title="Email of Rachel Meredith" href="mailto:Rachel.E.Meredith&#64;tn.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rachel.E.Meredith&#64;tn.gov</a> for any auxiliary aids or services needed to facilitate such participation. Contact may be in person, by writing, telephone, or other means, and should be made no less than 10 working days to allow time to provide such aid or services. Contact the State’s Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) Coordinator <span class="icon-mobile"></span>(1-866-253-5827) for further information. Hearing-impaired callers may use the Tennessee Relay Service <span class="icon-mobile"></span>(1-800-848-0298).</p>
<p>If it is hard for you to read, speak, or understand English, TDEC may be able to provide translation or interpretation services free of charge. Please contact <span class="icon-mobile"></span>(615) 532-0780 for more information.</p>
<p>If you would like to receive notices like this directly, contact the Public Participation Officer in the DLP’s Central Office for a Mailing List Request Form. Email <span class="icon-mail"></span><a title="Email for Solid Waste" href="mailto:Solid.Waste&#64;tn.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Solid.Waste&#64;tn.gov</a> or call <span class="icon-mobile"></span>(615) 552-8002.</p>

    
    

</div>


    
    
