    <div class="containers tn-accordion parbase">
    <div class="accordion" id="accordion-d8353c84534f4a03aed98bdfc84247c2">
        

        
            

            
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    

                    
                        <div class="accordion-heading">
                            <span class="accordion-title">
                                <button class="accordion-button icon-angle-right collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-d8353c84534f4a03aed98bdfc84247c2-0" aria-controls="collapse-d8353c84534f4a03aed98bdfc84247c2-0" aria-expanded="false">
                                    Occidental Chemical Corporation Class II Landfill Change of Ownership 
                                </button>
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <div id="collapse-d8353c84534f4a03aed98bdfc84247c2-0" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordion-d8353c84534f4a03aed98bdfc84247c2">
                            <div class="accordion-body panel-body" tabindex="0">
                                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <p>Environmental Resource Holdings, LLC, corporate successor to Occidental Chemical Corporation, has taken ownership of the existing Occidental Chemical Corporation Class II landfill. The Class II disposal facility is in post-closure care and located at 970 Santa Fe Pike, Columbia, TN 38401 (latitude 35.649007/longitude -87.049405). The Tennessee Department of Environment and Conservation’s (TDEC), Division of Land Protection – Waste Management Branch (DLP-WMB) approved a change in the identity of the owner for the Class II landfill, pursuant to Rule 0400-11-01-.02(6)(a) of Tennessee&#39;s Solid Waste Program Processing and Disposal Regulations. As part of this transfer of ownership identity, the facility name has not changed. The identity of the operator has changed from Occidental Chemical Corporation to Environmental Resource Holdings, LLC. The final decision to issue the permit modification was made on Thursday, June 9, 2026.</p>
<p>Paper copies may be reviewed at the TDEC Columbia Environmental Field Office at 1421 Hampshire Pike, Suite 100, Columbia, TN 38401 (931) 380-3371 and the TDEC DLP-WMB Central Office, Davy Crockett Tower, 500 James Robertson Parkway, 7th Floor, Nashville, TN 37243 (615) 532-0780. Questions or comments may be directed to the WMB Solid Waste Permitting Manager, Nickolaus Lytle, at the TDEC Central Office at <span class="icon-mail"></span><a title="Email Nick Lytle" href="mailto:Nickolaus.Lytle&#64;tn.gov">Nickolaus.Lytle&#64;tn.gov</a> or (615) 854-4581.</p>

    
    

</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-linkbuttons"><div>
	
        <div>
            
            
                <a href="/content/dam/tn/environment/solid-waste/documents/solid-waste/dlp_wmb_sw-chow-erh-final.pdf" target="_blank" class="button standard">Final Permit</a>
            
        
            
            
                <a href="https://dataviewers.tdec.tn.gov/dataviewers/f?p=19035:34051:::::P34051_PERMIT_ID:750" target="_blank" class="button standard">Dataviewer</a>
            
        </div>
	
</div></div>


</div>
