    <div class="containers tn-accordion parbase">
    <div class="accordion" id="accordion-c9de24fbad6140429eaaadc6b47090ff">
        

        
            

            
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    

                    
                        <div class="accordion-heading">
                            <span class="accordion-title">
                                <button class="accordion-button icon-angle-right collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-c9de24fbad6140429eaaadc6b47090ff-0" aria-controls="collapse-c9de24fbad6140429eaaadc6b47090ff-0" aria-expanded="false">
                                    Marion County Class I Landfill Permit Modification
                                </button>
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <div id="collapse-c9de24fbad6140429eaaadc6b47090ff-0" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordion-c9de24fbad6140429eaaadc6b47090ff">
                            <div class="accordion-body panel-body" tabindex="0">
                                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-textandimage textimage parbase">




<div class="textimage-text">
    
        <p>The Tennessee Department of Environment and Conservation (TDEC) has issued a permit major modification to the Marion County Government. The facility, identified as the Marion County Class I Landfill (SNL5800000197), is located in Marion County at 700 Chasey Simpson Road, Jasper, Tennessee (latitude 35.041667 N/longitude -85.627778 W). </p>
<p>This major modification corrected a construction deviation from the previous permit that resulted in the liner being constructed outside of the permitted waste limits. This major modification also resulted in an overall capacity decrease of 122,000 cubic yards to avoid conflicts with the existing transfer station at the site. This permit allows construction, operation, closure, and post-closure care of the Class I disposal facility for waste materials classified as domestic wastes, commercial wastes, institutional wastes, municipal solid wastes, bulky wastes, landscaping and land clearing wastes, industrial wastes, construction/demolition wastes, farming wastes, shredded automotive tires, dead animals, and/or certain wastes having similar characteristics and approved by TDEC. No hazardous wastes, as regulated by the Tennessee Hazardous Waste Management Act (Tennessee Code Annotated, Section 68-212-101, et. seq.) and the Rules adopted pursuant to the Act, shall be accepted for disposal at this facility.</p>
<p>Solid Waste made the draft of this permit available for review during a 45-day public comment period, which ended on January 26, 2026. Solid Waste received no oral or written comments during the above-mentioned public comment period.</p>

    
    

</div>


<div class="clear"></div></div>


    
    
